// Phase 2a (issue #1110): pins the *silent* side of the #1108 unchecked
// boundary. An `object` declaration is inert plumbing in Phase 1 -- it parses
// and type-checks without any verification obligation, and unlike proc /
// observer / resource it emits NO warning. With no `.pf.warn` sibling the
// imperative validate lane requires the run to be warning-free, so a future
// change that started warning on objects would fail here.
object Box<T> {
  var data : T
}
